== 2026-09-24T00:54:48Z paulzierep
## Small test v2 (post-fix run) — next blocker root-caused

Status after the IndexError fix (`904f649`): `small_test_v2` got through data augmentation and into training, then failed (exit 1, 43 s) with:

```
train_CLmodel.py", line 46, in <module> ... lengths[seq_id]
KeyError: 'BATS_SAMN07137077_METAG-scaffold_22978'
```

**Root cause (verified on disk):** `aug0_datacoverage_mean.tsv` in the run has **29,434 rows — every reference in the BAM header** — while the small run's input/augmented fasta has only **300 contigs**. `namelist` is read from that tsv (`get_augfeature.py:29`), but `lengths = get_length(.../aug0/sequences_aug0.fasta)` covers only the 300, so any BAM-only contig KeyErrors.

**Why the `47c1449` skip-fix didn't prevent it:** it filters `calculate_coverage_samplebyindex` (the aug1..N path), but the **aug0** coverage matrix is built by `calculate_coverage` via `gen_cov_from_bedout`, which walks the full bedtools genomecov output (all BAM references) and has no membership check against the input contig set.

**Related silent issue:** even where the crash is avoided, `namelist` (29,434) vs k-mer rows (300) means 29,134 `compositMat` rows are duplicates of row 0 after the `np.zeros` fix — so the contig-set filter must happen at the producer, not just crash-avoidance at the consumer.

**Plan (fix batch 2, branch `comebin-optimizations-v11`, one commit):** filter the aug0 coverage output to the input/augmented contig set (producer) + a defensive `namelist ∩ lengths` filter in `get_kmer_coverage`/`train_CLmodel` (consumer). Per docs/08 the validation is an end-to-end run on the small dataset — queued behind the active baseline rerun (`runs/baseline_rerun_autorestart1`, started 00:30 UTC, currently epoch 7/200), since no timed run may overlap a registered run.


