[0m$ [0mcd /vol/data/repos/metagenomic-binning-benchmark && gh issue create -R paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark --title "Baseline zero-bins failure chain: hmmer 3.4 vs pinned 3.1b2 poisons marker seed, unguarded cluster.py:368 read, wrapper masks the failure" --body "## What happened

The original pristine baseline (\`987db95\`, run \`baseline_unmodified\`) trained to epoch 175/200 but produced **zero bins and no evaluation**, and the wrapper's exit code did not reflect a failed binning stage. Root cause is a four-link failure chain, each link verified on disk.

## Failure chain (all links verified)

1. **Environment drift vs. the authors' pin.** \`comebin_env.yaml\` pins \`hmmer=3.1b2\`, but the live env had **hmmer 3.4**. \`hmmsearch --cut_tc\` against \`auxiliary/bacar_marker.hmm\` — a TC-less HMM — **hard-errors on 3.4** (zero hits), while **3.1b2 runs \`--cut_tc\` leniently and yields 2227 marker hits** (both measured directly).
2. **Stale empty outputs poison the resume path.** The failed run left 0-byte \`.bacar_marker.hmmout\`/\`.err\`/\`.out\` files (dated 2026-09-23 21:30). \`COMEBin/utils.py\` \`gen_seed\` skips hmmsearch when \`os.path.exists(hmmout)\` — so on any retry the empty file makes the step look done and **no seed is ever generated**.
3. **Unguarded read crashes the run.** \`COMEBin/cluster.py:368\` reads the marker seed unconditionally → \`FileNotFoundError\` after hours of training.
4. **Wrapper masks the failure.** \`run_comebin.sh\` swallowed the clustering/get_result exit status, so the run could be recorded as successful while bins were missing. Our baseline runner now traps a missing bins dir and forces \`rc=1\` ([\`8bb73dd\`](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/commit/8bb73dd)).

A secondary crash on the same path: sklearn ≥1.0 removed \`KMeans(n_jobs=...)\` (and the private \`sklearn.cluster._kmeans\` import), so clustering died with \`TypeError\` even once seeds existed — fixed as COMEBin commit [\`358ddd8\`](https://github.com/paulzierep/COMEBin/commit/358ddd8) (also [\`c8f22e4\`](https://github.com/paulzierep/COMEBin/commit/c8f22e4) on \`comebin-small-fix\`).

## Resolution

* Env downgraded to **hmmer 3.1b2** (only package changed; before/after \`micromamba list\` snapshots in \`runs/baseline_rerun_autorestart1/logs/env_list_{before,after}_hmmerfix.txt\`).
* Baseline runner gained \`BENCHMARK_RESUME=1\` (fresh seed regeneration, phase-1 archiving, bins-missing trap, \`hmmsearch\` version stamp) — benchmark-repo commit \`8bb73dd\`.
* sklearn KMeans compat fix: COMEBin \`358ddd8\` / \`c8f22e4\`.
* **Verified end-to-end:** rerun \`baseline_rerun_autorestart1\` completed 200/200 epochs (99.19% Top1), clustering + \`get_result\` produced **60 bins**, CheckM2 mean 25.01% completeness / 2.98% contamination.

## Upstream status

COMEBin **v1.1.0** already mitigates link 1+2 with \`_hmm_models_have_tc_cutoffs()\\` → falls back to \`-E 1e-5\` when TC cutoffs are absent (plus empty-cache/seed guards), so \`comebin-optimizations-v11\` is immune to this chain. The remaining gap upstream is the unguarded seed read / wrapper exit masking, which is why the fix chain above is kept on our branches.

Related eval-side environment issue: the standalone CheckM v1 env (Python 3.14) breaks \`lineage_wf\` worker pickling; eval now uses the CheckM v1 in the COMEBin env (Python 3.10) + \`LD_LIBRARY_PATH\` — see \`scripts/run_eval.sh\`." 2>&1 | tail -3
